# Indent checks and commits

## Python under `churn-prediction/`

From the **workspace root**, before treating Python edits as done, run:

```powershell
python -m tabnanny churn-prediction
python -m compileall -q churn-prediction
```

Fix any reported issues. Omit `-q` on `compileall` if file-by-file output helps.

## Commit messages

Use conventional-style messages:

```text
<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary under ~72 chars>

- Optional detail bullets
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `chore`, `test`. Prefer a small scope (`churn-prediction`, `readme`, etc.).

When suggesting or writing commit text for the user, follow that shape.

Full context: [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). Human-oriented copy also lives in [README.md](README.md) (*Check indentation & structured commits*).
